                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1877ffe8-2f25-4028-af1e-d2d267a1cd06",
                                                "sense_id": "a6b53489-8fae-3797-9d68-c7fabe04608b",
                                                "text": "When, across the hundredfold poor scepticisms, trivialisms and constitutional cobwebberies of Dryasdust, you catch any glimpse of a William the Conqueror, a Tancred of Hauteville or suchlike, — do you not discern veritably some rude outline of a true God-made King […]?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "943370f6-15ef-4f7d-ae91-d0cb6ad78fc8",
                                                "sense_id": "a6b53489-8fae-3797-9d68-c7fabe04608b",
                                                "text": "As per the old Jewish joke “ask two Jews, get three opinions”, there’s room on this seven-strong bill (plus [Hannah] Gadsby) for at least that many different perspectives on gender – including some impish scepticism from Canadian comic DeAnne Smith, who complains about “getting they/them’d against my will since 2005”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
